  "id": "COMPOUND:1010 - DISEASE:1932",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between methoxyflurane and Macrostomia, mediated through the coiled-coil domain containing 33 (CCD33) protein. Methoxyflurane is shown to affect CCD33, which in turn is implicated in multiple conditions, including Hypophosphatemic rickets, Melanoma-Pancreatic cancer syndrome, and Glaucoma 1, open angle, O. These conditions are all linked to CCD33 through a causal pathway, and CCD33 is directly associated with Macrostomia. The shared involvement of CCD33 in multiple pathophysiological processes implies a possible mechanism by which methoxyflurane could influence macrostomia, though the exact nature of this mechanism remains to be elucidated. The evidence is consistent across multiple paths, suggesting a plausible, though not yet fully understood, mechanistic link between methoxyflurane and Macrostomia.",
